Fix `push-rootfs-part.py --check` false MISMATCH on the phone

The `--check` path streams 128 MiB and has the phone md5 it. BusyBox `md5sum` prints
`<hash>  -` when reading from stdin (two fields), but the parser only accepted a
single 32-char field, so `phone_md5` was always empty and the check reported MISMATCH
even on a perfect transfer. Match on the first field instead.

Tested against `BusyBox v1.38.0` on the phone; the write path was never affected.

--- a/linux-kit/push-rootfs-part.py
+++ b/linux-kit/push-rootfs-part.py
@@ -180,9 +180,12 @@ def main():
         phone_md5 = ""
         for line in res.get("out", "").splitlines():
-            if len(line.split()) == 1 and len(line.strip()) == 32:
-                phone_md5 = line.strip()
+            # BusyBox md5sum prints "hash  -" when reading stdin, so match the first token
+            toks = line.split()
+            if toks and len(toks[0]) == 32:
+                phone_md5 = toks[0]
+                break
         say("host  md5: %s" % host_md5)
         say("phone md5: %s" % phone_md5)
         say("MATCH" if host_md5 == phone_md5 else "MISMATCH")
